From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:09:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vkms: take a writeback job's vblank reference once the
 CRTC is on

A writeback commit that enables the CRTC never completed. The job's
vblank reference was taken in prepare_writeback_job(), before the commit
enables the CRTC. A CRTC that is off holds the private reference that
drm_crtc_vblank_off() takes ("prevent drm_vblank_get"), so
drm_crtc_vblank_get() returned -EINVAL there, nobody looked at the
result, and drm_crtc_vblank_on_config() found no user and left the
vblank timer stopped. The composer, which signals the job's fence, runs
only from that timer, so the fence never signalled; the job stayed first
in the connector's queue, and every later job's completion signalled it
instead of its own. The cleanup then dropped a reference it never held.

A device whose CRTC is already on at the first commit does not show it,
as the module's default device, whose fbdev client enables the CRTC. A
device made through configfs starts with its CRTC off: the first commit
timed out at the fence even for a 2D mode, and so did every commit after
it.

Count the composer user in prepare_writeback_job(), as the previous
patch of this group does, because every prepared job is cleaned up. Take
the vblank reference in atomic_commit(), where the CRTC is on, keep
whether it was taken in the job, put it in the cleanup, and complete the
job with the error if the reference cannot be taken. The CRC source
keeps vkms_set_composer(), which holds a reference of its own.

The KUnit fixture now enables vblank handling and uses the driver's
commit tail like a real device, because the default commit tail waits
for vblanks and starts the timer on its own. The new tests commit a
writeback job with the CRTC off and with it on, for a 2D mode and for
each stereo layout, and fail when the job does not complete.

Fixes: drm/vkms: keep the composer running for every writeback job
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
